"hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1190,"Yahya bin Hakim narrated to us, Abu Amer narrated to us, Saeed bin Abdul Aziz Al-Tanukhi narrated to us, he said: I heard Suleiman bin Musa speaking, h. Muhammad bin Muammar narrated it, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Sufyan, He said: When death befell him, he was severely distressed. He said: My sister, Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan, told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “Whoever prays four rak’ahs,” and Ibn Muammar said: “Whoever prays four rak’ahs before noon and four after it, God will make him forbidden.” ""on fire"""
1191,"Nasr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Amr i.e. Ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, Sadaqah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man ibn Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs four rak’ahs before the prayer Al-Hijr, and four after that he will be forbidden to Hell.”"
1192,"Nasr bin Marzuq told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Al-Haytham, meaning Ibn Humaid, told us, Al-Nu’man, meaning Ibn al-Mundhir, told us about Makhoul, on the authority of Anbasa, on the authority of Umm Habibah, that she told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is equal to something like it."
